```javascript
function calculateSquareRoot(num) {
  if (num < 0) return NaN;
  if (num === 0) return 0;
  let x = num;
  while (true) {
    const new_x = (x + num / x) / 2;
    if (Math.abs(new_x - x) < 0.000001) return new_x;
    x = new_x;
  }
}
```

this uses the Babylonian method for computing square roots — an iterative method that keeps improving the estimate using `x_(n+1) = (x_n + num / x_n) / 2`. the loop keeps going until the difference between the current estimate and the previous one drops below a small epsilon (here, `0.000001`), wan~
